	Well, you need to do a few things to configure nethack for
your system.  Because it is so widely used, it has to accomodate a
whole bunch of different types of systems, it requires system
customization, and it also requires you to tell it where you want
things.
	What you need to do is this:  go to the sys/unix directory and
read Install.unx.  then you run setup.sh to set everything else in the
tree up for unix (which is generally the default, explaining your good
compile the first time).  Then follow the instructions in the
Install.unx file.  They list the files you need to customize, and are
relatively straightforward.  When you are finally ready, it will tell
you to go do a make.  Have some coffee ready 8).
	good luck -- feel free to mail me if you need help with any
particulars.  I've recompiled the damn thing several times already 8).

